SUMMARY:Deadline: Hugo Burge Foundation: Grants for Creative Individuals 20
 26
DESCRIPTION:Project grants from the Hugo Burge Foundation\, a major UK arts
  funder that distributed GBP 400\,000 in its first full year (2025) across
  three funds: Creative Education (0-29 year olds)\, Creative Communities (
 organisations\, festivals\, community groups)\, and Creative Individuals. 
 The Creative Individuals Fund (GBP 50\,000 available in 2026) is open to i
 ndividuals seeking support for the development of artistic projects or pra
 ctice\; it awards up to GBP 5\,000 and can fund the entire project. Practi
 tioners in all creative disciplines across the UK may apply. The Foundatio
 n also runs a GBP 7\,000 access support fund (first-come\, first-served) t
 hat pays access support workers up to GBP 300 for a day's services for app
 licants facing barriers to applying\, including those who are Deaf\, disab
 led\, or neurodivergent (no proof required). ELIGIBILITY: practitioners in
  all creative disciplines based across the UK. Applications are submitted 
 via Submittable and close 31 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Hugo Burge Founda
 tion\nLocation: United Kingdom\nAward: Up to GBP 5\,000 per individual (ca
 n fund up to 100% of a project under GBP 10\,000). No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Per project\n\nMore: https://www.hugoburgefoundation.org/grants?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
