UID:nakanojo-biennale-2027-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260712
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260713
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nakanojo Biennale 2027: International Artist Open Call (G
 unma Prefecture\, Japan)
DESCRIPTION:Nakanojo Biennale 2027 (11th edition) is an international open 
 call for artists of all genres — sculpture\, painting\, photography\, vi
 deo art\, installation\, performance\, and more — to exhibit in Nakanojo
  Town\, Gunma Prefecture\, Japan. Theme: 'Echoing Green'\, inspired by Wil
 liam Blake's poem\, exploring cycles of life\, regeneration\, and connecti
 on between past and future generations. Open internationally to individual
  artists and artist groups at all career stages\; new participants are enc
 ouraged. A production grant is provided (amount not publicly specified)\; 
 no exhibition or residency fees are charged. Residency accommodation avail
 able from April 2027. Staff support provided for venue selection and insta
 llation guidance. First-time participants in Japan must attend an on-site 
 venue inspection\; an online orientation on 5 September 2026 is required f
 or all accepted artists. Deadline: 12 July 2026 at 23:59 JST (online). App
 ly via Google Form at https://forms.gle/SS8DaaGA6uwUKogj7. Full details at
  https://nakanojo-biennale.com/2027-open-call/english.html. Contact: offic
 e@nakanojo-biennale.com.\n\nOrganisation: Nakanojo Biennale Executive Comm
 ittee / Nakanojo Town\, Gunma Prefecture\nLocation: Nakanojo Town\, Gunma 
 Prefecture\, Japan\nAward: Production grant provided (amount not specified
  publicly). No exhibition fee\, no residency fee. Insurance subsidies avai
 lable. Artists responsible for materials\, food\, transportation\, and ins
 tallation/removal costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Exhibition: 18 Sep
 tember – 24 October 2027 (37 days). Production period: April–August 20
 27. Residency accommodation available from April 2027.\n\nMore: https://na
 kanojo-biennale.com/2027-open-call/english.html?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nakanojo-biennale.com/2027-open-call/english.html?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nakanojo Town\, Gunma Prefecture\, Japan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oif-artist-mobility-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: OIF: Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultu
 ral Goods 2026 (Francophonie)
DESCRIPTION:The OIF Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultural
  Goods programme provides grants of up to EUR 5\,000 for mobility (travel\
 , accommodation\, visa fees\, logistics) and up to EUR 2\,500 for circulat
 ion of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs) within the Fran
 cophone zone\; both can be combined. ELIGIBILITY: professional artists and
  established artistic collectives with a demonstrated connection to the Fr
 ancophone space (by nationality\, working language\, or artistic collabora
 tions)\, residing in an OIF member state\, with minimum 2 years of experie
 nce in the cultural or artistic sector\; must directly manage the project 
 (not act as intermediaries)\; one application per individual per call. ELI
 GIBLE DISCIPLINES: live performance (music\, theatre\, dance\, comedy\, st
 orytelling)\, cinema/audiovisual\, literature/publishing\, and visual arts
 . PRIORITY given to projects promoting gender equality\, women artists\, c
 reators under 35\, and South-South mobility. Projects must take place betw
 een 25 March and 30 November 2026. Multiple selection sessions throughout 
 the year\; call open until 31 August 2026. Information webinars: 11 March\
 , 13 May\, and 8 July 2026 at 3 PM Paris time. Contact: culture.dlc@franco
 phonie.org. Apply at https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicatio
 ns/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Organisation internationale de la Francophonie (OIF)\nLocation: Fra
 ncophone zone (OIF member states globally)\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 for ar
 tist mobility (travel\, accommodation\, visas\, logistics). Up to EUR 2\,5
 00 for circulation of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs).
  Both can be combined. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies or tours
  of 5 days to 3 months. Projects must take place between 25 March and 30 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nMore: https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicat
 ions/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applications/soutien-a-la-ci
 rculation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Francophone zone (OIF member states globally)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bfi-doc-society-made-of-truth-short-film-fund@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260702
SUMMARY:Deadline: BFI Doc Society: Made of Truth – Short Non-Fiction Film
  Fund (UK)
DESCRIPTION:BFI Doc Society's Made of Truth fund supports early-career UK f
 ilmmakers making non-fiction live-action or animated short films of 5–40
  minutes. Up to 13 projects are funded per annual round. AMOUNT: up to £2
 5\,000 per project. ELIGIBILITY: early-career directors and producers who 
 are UK residents\; teams must have at least two people (a producer and a d
 irector)\; directors cannot have received a commercial distribution deal f
 or a non-fiction feature in the last five years\; a reasonable proportion 
 of early-career crew is required. Applications must meet at least three of
  six priorities: equity/diversity/inclusion\, audience impact\, talent dev
 elopment\, creative risk\, UK-wide access\, and environmental sustainabili
 ty. OPENS: 18 May 2026 at 1pm UK time. DEADLINE: 1 July 2026 at 1pm UK tim
 e. APPLY via the BFI Doc Society website. Contact: hellobfi@docsociety.org
 .\n\nOrganisation: BFI Doc Society\nLocation: UK (both director and produc
 er must be UK residents)\nAward: Up to £25\,000 non-recoupable grant. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: Short films 5–40 minutes\; up to 13 projects
  funded per year\n\nMore: https://bfi.docsociety.org/funds/made-of-truth?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://bfi.docsociety.org/funds/made-of-truth?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK (both director and producer must be UK residents)
