BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:samstag-international-visual-arts-scholarship-2027@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260701
SUMMARY:Deadline: Samstag International Visual Arts Scholarships - Class of
  2027
DESCRIPTION:The Samstag International Visual Arts Scholarships are annual s
 cholarships enabling Australian artists to develop their artistic capaciti
 es through a dedicated year of practice-based learning at an international
  institution of their choice. AMOUNT: AUD $75\,000 tax-exempt stipend\; in
 stitutional fees for one academic year (where applicable)\; return airfare
 s\; and travel and health insurance. ELIGIBILITY: Australian citizens or p
 ermanent residents aged 18 or over who are either (a) currently enrolled i
 n a practice-led visual arts program at an Australian institution of highe
 r education\, having successfully completed at least two years of an under
 graduate or postgraduate degree\; or (b) graduates of a practice-led visua
 l arts undergraduate or postgraduate qualification at an Australian instit
 ution of higher education (graduates of more than five years' standing are
  now eligible following 2023 guideline updates). PROCESS: applicants must 
 create an account in the online portal\, download the Samstag Microsoft Po
 werPoint template\, read the Class of 2027 Guidelines\, and complete and s
 ubmit the online application form. Accounts can be created before the dead
 line and applications saved for later submission. Prior applicants (Classe
 s of 2024\, 2025\, or 2026) can reuse the same account. Deadline: 30 June 
 2026\, midnight Australian Central Standard Time (ACST). Apply at https://
 samstag.adelaide.edu.au/scholarship/apply/.\n\nOrganisation: Samstag Museu
 m of Art\, University of South Australia\nLocation: Australia (applicants 
 must be Australian citizens or permanent residents)\; 12-month placement a
 t an international institution of the scholar's choice.\nAward: AUD $75\,0
 00 tax-exempt stipend\; institutional fees for one academic year of study 
 (where applicable)\; return airfares\; and travel and health insurance. No
  application fee.\nDuration: 12 months overseas at an international learni
 ng institution.\n\nMore: https://samstag.adelaide.edu.au/scholarship/apply
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://samstag.adelaide.edu.au/scholarship/apply/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia (applicants must be Australian citizens or permanent res
 idents)\; 12-month placement at an international institution of the schola
 r's choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:freelands-learning-through-making-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260912
SUMMARY:Deadline: Freelands Foundation: Learning Through Making Fund
DESCRIPTION:The Learning Through Making fund supports UK-based visual art o
 rganisations to bring opportunities for making and material exploration in
 to their art education work. Freelands Foundation is looking for explorato
 ry projects that embrace openness\, collaboration\, and iteration -- enabl
 ing organisations to work with materials in an expansive way\, unpicking p
 reconceptions about making and material literacy without predefined outcom
 es. ELIGIBLE ACTIVITIES: providing materials\, transport\, or access to ex
 pertise and facilities\; action-research trials such as a new series of wo
 rkshops or events developing material literacy\; adding a making-focused e
 lement to existing activity. Projects may range from a few days to several
  months\, but must take place between 1 January and 31 December 2027. AMOU
 NT: up to £25\,000\; funding provided no earlier than December 2026. ELIG
 IBILITY: UK-based visual art organisations run with a charitable purpose a
 nd for public benefit\; eligible types include charities registered in Eng
 land and Wales\, Scotland\, or Northern Ireland\; exempt charities\; galle
 ries\, museums\, or organisations within a Local Authority or larger chari
 table body (e.g. universities)\; and Community Interest Companies or Commu
 nity Benefit Societies meeting specific criteria (charitable purposes\, as
 set lock\, no dividend distribution\, ability to segregate restricted fund
 s). Organisations with a prior Freelands Foundation grant relationship are
  eligible\; you may not apply for activity already funded by Freelands Fou
 ndation. Individuals are not eligible. HOW TO APPLY: download the Applicat
 ion Form\, Application Guidance\, and optional Access Form from freelandsf
 oundation.co.uk\; email completed form to grants@freelandsfoundation.co.uk
  with subject line 'LTM Fund - Application'\; one additional page of image
 s or diagrams may be included. APPLICATION SUPPORT SESSIONS (online): 9 Ju
 ly 2026\, 10:30am-12pm\; 12 August 2026\, 10:30am-12pm. KEY DATES: applica
 tions open 17 June 2026\; close 11 September 2026 at 12pm\; outcomes share
 d 23 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Freelands Foundation\nLocation: UK (E
 ngland\, Northern Ireland\, Scotland\, Wales)\; activity must occur within
  the United Kingdom.\nAward: Up to £25\,000. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: Projects of any length\, taking place between 1 January and 31 December
  2027. Funding provided no earlier than December 2026.\n\nMore: https://fr
 eelandsfoundation.co.uk/engage/apply/grants/learning-through-making-fund?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://freelandsfoundation.co.uk/engage/apply/grants/learning-through-
 making-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK (England\, Northern Ireland\, Scotland\, Wales)\; activity must
  occur within the United Kingdom.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:phenomenon-grant-kerenidis-pepe-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Phenomenon Grant 2026 (Second Edition)
DESCRIPTION:Created in 2025\, the Phenomenon Grant is a yearly program that
  supports art projects in Greece with grants of EUR 5\,000 to EUR 10\,000 
 for individuals\, collectives\, and non-profit organizations engaged with 
 queer\, feminist\, anti-colonial\, and other emancipatory art practices. T
 he grant aims to support critical phases of artistic development\, enablin
 g experimentation\, research\, collaboration\, and the realization of new 
 and ongoing projects. In a context marked by rising authoritarianism\, gen
 ocidal forces and the dismantling of social justice advancements\, the pro
 gram seeks to support voices that critically and ethically engage with the
 se issues\, create spaces of resistance\, reimagine futures beyond exclusi
 on\, persecution\, and domination\, and open pathways toward collective li
 beration. Particular attention is paid to collaborative endeavours rooted 
 in Greece that are built on connections with the Global Majority\, promoti
 ng networks of translocal solidarity and interconnected struggles. Organiz
 ed and supported by Kerenidis Pepe\, which has pledged a total budget of E
 UR 60\,000 over 2025-2027\, the amount awarded is based on the application
 's actual funding needs. In 2025 the program received 193 applications and
  awarded three grants of EUR 8\,500 each to Athens Museum of Queer Arts (A
 MOQA)\, Forensic Architecture Initiative Athens (FAIA) and Theo Panagopoul
 os. The 2026 selection committee is composed of Athena Athanasiou\, Dora G
 arcia\, Christina Li\, VASKOS\, and chaired by Aggelika Mitsiou. The submi
 ssion period runs from 1 September to 30 September 2026\, with selected pr
 ojects announced in November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Phenomenon Association
 \, supported by Kerenidis Pepe\nLocation: Greece (projects rooted in Greec
 e)\nAward: Grants ranging from EUR 5\,000 to EUR 10\,000\, based on the ap
 plication's actual funding needs. Each edition awards a minimum of EUR 20\
 ,000 to two to four grantees (in 2025\, three grants of EUR 8\,500 each we
 re awarded).\nDuration: One- or two-year initiatives\; selected projects a
 nnounced November 2026\n\nMore: https://kerenidispepe.art/projects/grants/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://kerenidispepe.art/projects/grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Greece (projects rooted in Greece)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mountainfilm-commitment-grants-emerging-filmmaker-fellowship-2026@artif
 icialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260717
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mountainfilm: Commitment Grants & Emerging Filmmaker Fell
 owship
DESCRIPTION:Mountainfilm's Commitment Grants support documentary filmmakers
  with projects in post-production\, with over USD 90\,000 in funding this 
 cycle for films that celebrate adventure\, activism\, social justice\, cul
 ture\, the environment\, and indomitable spirit. Mountainfilm actively enc
 ourages diversity behind the camera\, and a portion of funding is set asid
 e for two focus areas: projects featuring an LGBTQ+ protagonist or a story
  about overcoming personal challenges\, societal stigmas\, and/or communit
 y obstacles with a meaningful connection to the outdoors or nature-based p
 ursuits\; and projects exploring immigration or migration\, or created by 
 immigrant or first-generation immigrant filmmakers. AWARDS: individual Com
 mitment Grants range from USD 3\,000 to 6\,000. EMERGING FILMMAKER FELLOWS
 HIP: one early-career filmmaker is selected from the Commitment Grant appl
 icant pool for a yearlong mentorship that includes edit and story consulta
 tion\, networking opportunities\, a cash award\, and a funded trip to Tell
 uride during the festival over Memorial Day weekend (travel\, lodging\, an
 d a Mountainfilm pass\, applicable to the year following the award). ELIGI
 BILITY: Commitment Grants are open to applicants from any country\; the Em
 erging Filmmaker Fellowship accepts applicants from any country but requir
 es current U.S. residency. Post-production projects only\, completed\, rel
 eased\, or festival-screened projects are not eligible\, and impact campai
 gns are not funded. Prior Commitment Grant recipients should not re-apply 
 for the same project\; previously declined projects may re-apply only with
  substantial changes. REQUIREMENTS: a video sample or trailer of the curre
 nt project no longer than 10 minutes (password-protected Vimeo links prefe
 rred)\; the screener link must stay active and cannot be changed after sub
 mission. The Emerging Filmmaker application additionally requires a direct
 or bio\, headshot\, and cover letter. Recipients are expected to provide p
 rogress updates 2-3 times a year\, include Mountainfilm recognition in cre
 dits\, and discuss premiere consideration with the programming team. TIMEL
 INE: applications are open July 1 to July 16\, 2026 (closing 11:59 PM MDT)
 \, with notifications in late August or early September. Questions: entrie
 s@mountainfilm.org.\n\nOrganisation: Mountainfilm\nLocation: Application o
 nline\; Telluride\, Colorado\, United States (fellowship trip during the f
 estival). Commitment Grants are open to filmmakers from any country\; the 
 Emerging Filmmaker Fellowship requires current U.S. residency.\nAward: Ove
 r USD 90\,000 in total funding. Individual Commitment Grants range from US
 D 3\,000 to 6\,000. The Emerging Filmmaker Fellowship adds a yearlong ment
 orship\, a cash award\, and a funded trip to Telluride over Memorial Day w
 eekend (travel\, lodging\, and a festival pass).\nDuration: Commitment Gra
 nts support projects in post-production\; the Emerging Filmmaker Fellowshi
 p is a yearlong mentorship.\n\nMore: https://www.mountainfilm.org/mountain
 film-initiatives/commitment-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mountainfilm.org/mountainfilm-initiatives/commitment-grants
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Application online\; Telluride\, Colorado\, United States (fellows
 hip trip during the festival). Commitment Grants are open to filmmakers fr
 om any country\; the Emerging Filmmaker Fellowship requires current U.S. r
 esidency.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-publication-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260730
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260731
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Publication
DESCRIPTION:The Mondriaan Fund's Publication grant supports the production 
 of special publications about living visual artists from the Netherlands o
 r the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. It funds books and other publications
  that give substantial\, high-quality attention to an artist's work and pr
 actice. WHO CAN APPLY: visual artists and publishers\, individually or joi
 ntly\; the featured artist(s) must be professional and have been active fo
 r at least one year\, based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of th
 e Kingdom. AMOUNT: the Mondriaan Fund contributes a maximum of 35% of the 
 eligible expenses\; the available budget for this round is EUR 205\,000. A
 PPLYING: submitted through the Mondriaan Fund's online application portal\
 , which requires a pre-created account (allow several working days to set 
 up). DEADLINE: 30 July 2026\, 16:00 Dutch time (10:00 Caribbean time).\n\n
 Organisation: Mondriaan Fund (Mondriaan Fonds)\nLocation: Netherlands. Fea
 tured artist(s) must be professional visual artists based in the Netherlan
 ds or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; publishers may co-apply.\nAward:
  Contribution of up to 35% of eligible expenses. Total budget for this rou
 nd is EUR 205\,000.\nDuration: Project-based (production of a publication)
 .\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/publi
 cation-2/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/publication-2
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Featured artist(s) must be professional visual artist
 s based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; publishe
 rs may co-apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Mondriaan Fund's Residency grant supports professional visu
 al artists\, curators\, and art observers who want to deepen their practic
 e through a residency in the Netherlands or abroad. It contributes to the 
 costs of a self-arranged residency that offers meaningful development for 
 the applicant's work. WHO CAN APPLY: visual artists\, curators\, and art o
 bservers who have been professionally active for at least one year and are
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. AMOUNT: th
 e grant amount varies depending on the residency's location and duration\;
  applicants must contribute at least 10% of the costs themselves\, through
  personal investment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\,
  or crowdfunding. APPLYING: submitted through the Mondriaan Fund's online 
 application portal\, which requires a pre-created account (allow several w
 orking days). DEADLINE: 27 August 2026\, 16:00 Dutch time (11:00 Caribbean
  time).\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund (Mondriaan Fonds)\nLocation: Nethe
 rlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part 
 of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherlands or abroad.\
 nAward: Grant amount varies depending on the location and duration of the 
 residency. Applicants must contribute at least 10% themselves (personal in
 vestment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\, or crowdfun
 ding).\nDuration: Varies by residency.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds
 .nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Ca
 ribbean part of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherland
 s or abroad.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:doc-society-climate-story-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260824
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260825
SUMMARY:Deadline: Doc Society: Climate Story Fund
DESCRIPTION:The Doc Society Climate Story Fund\, run by Doc Society's Clima
 te Story Unit\, provides grants of up to USD 125\,000 to support non-ficti
 on projects in late production and the implementation of impact campaigns 
 for both completed and in-production projects. The fund supports compellin
 g independent media storytelling and impact strategies aligned with the Fu
 nd's mission around climate justice and biodiversity. This call has no set
  theme\, welcoming applications across all areas aligned with the Fund's m
 ission. Since 2021 the fund has distributed more than USD 4M to over 50 pr
 ojects\, with grantee work reaching distribution through outlets including
  BBC\, POV\, Netflix\, Hulu\, Disney+\, Spotify\, YouTube\, and WhatsApp. 
 WHAT YOU GET: up to USD 125\,000 to support non-fiction projects in late p
 roduction and impact campaigns. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: open to filmmakers of any
  nationality. DEADLINE: 24 August 2026. TO APPLY: see the fund page and ap
 ply via the Doc Society application. Questions: climate@docsociety.org.\n\
 nOrganisation: Doc Society (Climate Story Unit)\nLocation: Remote / intern
 ational. Open to filmmakers of any nationality.\nAward: Grants of up to US
 D 125\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Supports late-production of non
 -fiction projects and the implementation of impact campaigns for completed
  and in-production projects.\n\nMore: https://climatestoryunit.org/fund/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://climatestoryunit.org/fund/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / international. Open to filmmakers of any nationality.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prospect-art-new-work-we-come-in-pieces-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:Deadline: Prospect Art: NEW WORK Commission 2027 - "We Come in Piec
 es"
DESCRIPTION:Prospect Art invites visual artists worldwide to apply for the 
 2027 NEW WORK commission\, a USD 1\,500 project grant supporting the creat
 ion of a new\, conceptually driven work responding to the curatorial theme
  "We Come in Pieces\," developed by 2026-2027 Curatorial Fellow Alma Samme
 l. Through a single application\, artists are also considered for ONE WORK
  (an online series featuring an in-depth conversation centered on a single
  completed artwork) and BROADCAST (a curated online program of screenings\
 , artist talks\, and discussions). THEME: "We Come in Pieces" proposes the
  Alien as a method for shifting perspective\, approaching alienness as a p
 ractice of estrangement to encounter the world beyond familiar human-cente
 red narratives. It explores relationships between human and more-than-huma
 n worlds\, speculative cosmologies\, ecological systems\, technologies\, l
 andscapes\, histories\, infrastructures\, and nonhuman forms of intelligen
 ce (satellites and orbital debris\, fungal networks\, oceans\, atmospheric
  systems\, algorithmic intelligences)\, inviting works that displace the p
 oint of listening\, seeing\, sensing\, or knowing. Research-based and conc
 eptually driven practices are especially encouraged. WHAT'S OFFERED: NEW W
 ORK\, USD 1\,500 to one artist plus a featured website section and social 
 promotion (project completed within 12 months)\; ONE WORK\, a published ar
 ticle and social promotion\; BROADCAST\, a USD 125 screening or speaking f
 ee and inclusion in a themed program. ELIGIBILITY: professional visual art
 ists working in any medium at any career stage\, except those currently en
 rolled in undergraduate or graduate studio art programs\; collectives may 
 apply. Media welcomed include moving image\, installation\, sculpture\, ph
 otography\, performance\, sound\, digital media\, social practice\, and in
 terdisciplinary forms. APPLICATION: submit via the official Google Form wi
 th contact information\, a project description (250 words)\, a sketch/visu
 alization (1-3 images)\, up to 3 links to completed work samples\, a state
 ment relating the project to the theme (200 words)\, a short bio and exhib
 ition history (500 words)\, and a budget breakdown of the USD 1\,500. A US
 D 10 administrative fee is paid via PayPal (include PayPal name and transa
 ction ID)\; a fee waiver is available with no explanation by emailing subm
 issions@prospectart.org before the deadline. Writers may email gioj@prospe
 ctart.org with samples. DEADLINE: 16 August 2026\; results for the NEW WOR
 K grant notified by end of September. INFO SESSION: 5 August 2026 at noon 
 PST.\n\nOrganisation: Prospect Art\nLocation: Remote / online. Open to vis
 ual artists worldwide\; programs (ONE WORK\, BROADCAST) run online.\nAward
 : NEW WORK: USD 1\,500 commission for one artist\, plus a featured website
  section and social promotion. BROADCAST: USD 125 screening or speaking fe
 e if selected. ONE WORK: a published article (exposure). NOTE: a USD 10 ad
 ministrative fee applies to apply\, with a no-questions-asked waiver avail
 able on request before the deadline. PayPal account required to receive fu
 nds.\nDuration: The commissioned NEW WORK project should be completed with
 in twelve months of selection.\n\nMore: https://www.prospectart.org/new-wo
 rk-grant?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.prospectart.org/new-work-grant?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / online. Open to visual artists worldwide\; programs (ONE 
 WORK\, BROADCAST) run online.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fujifilm-gfx-challenge-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:Deadline: FUJIFILM GFX Challenge Grant Program 2026
DESCRIPTION:The GFX Challenge Grant Program\, sponsored by FUJIFILM and run
 ning since 2021\, awards 5 Global Grant Awards (USD 10\,000) and 10 Region
 al Grant Awards (USD 5\,000) to help aspiring creatives bring imaging proj
 ects to life. It is designed to nurture emerging and promising content cre
 ators\, giving them the opportunity to create content on topics with signi
 ficant meaning to them while gaining experience with FUJIFILM GFX System g
 ear\, including the GFX ETERNA 55 filmmaking camera. Proposed projects may
  be submitted as still photography or in movie format. AWARDS: both tiers 
 include complimentary use of a GFX System camera body and two GF lenses fo
 r the duration of the project\, plus mentoring and technical assistance fr
 om Fujifilm technicians and product experts. At the end of the production 
 period in May 2027\, recipients' final content is showcased on fujifilm-x.
 com\, with a series of exhibitions planned in various countries. ELIGIBILI
 TY: open to both amateur and professional photographers and videographers 
 who are residents of the countries/regions listed in the Entry Submission 
 section of the program page\; not open to employees or officers of FUJIFIL
 M and its subsidiaries. TO APPLY: combine three items into a single PDF: (
 1) the preformatted cover letter (downloadable from the program page)\; (2
 ) the project proposal covering descriptive plan\, objectives\, evaluation
  and outcome measures\, communications\, how you will use the Fujifilm par
 tnership and mentoring\, schedule\, and budget\; (3) a portfolio for each 
 individual involved. Proposals must be in English (optionally accompanied 
 by a version in your own language\; language proficiency is not judged). E
 ntry period 16 June to 17 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: FUJIFILM\nLocation
 : Open to residents of the countries/regions listed under Entry Submission
  on the program page. Final content showcased on fujifilm-x.com plus plann
 ed exhibitions in various countries.\nAward: 5 Global Grant Awards of USD 
 10\,000 and 10 Regional Grant Awards of USD 5\,000. All recipients also ge
 t complimentary use of a GFX System camera body (including the FUJIFILM GF
 X ETERNA 55 filmmaking camera) and two GF lenses for the duration of the p
 roject\, plus mentoring and technical assistance from Fujifilm technicians
  and product experts. Total approximate retail value of all awards: USD 22
 9\,500. No purchase necessary\; no entry fee.\nDuration: Application windo
 w 16 June to 17 August 2026. Production period concludes in May 2027\, aft
 er which final content is showcased on fujifilm-x.com and in a planned ser
 ies of exhibitions.\n\nMore: https://www.fujifilm-x.com/global/gfx-challen
 ge-grant-program/year-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://www.fujifilm-x.com/global/gfx-challenge-grant-program/year-2026
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open to residents of the countries/regions listed under Entry Subm
 ission on the program page. Final content showcased on fujifilm-x.com plus
  planned exhibitions in various countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fundacion-ama-amoedo-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260909
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260910
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fundacion Ama Amoedo Grants 2026 (4th edition)
DESCRIPTION:The Fundacion Ama Amoedo Grants provide resources and opportuni
 ties to strengthen the visual arts ecosystem and its institutions. Through
  an open call\, ten grants of USD 10\,000 are awarded annually across four
  categories: Artists\, Art and Social Engagement\, Organizations\, and Pub
 lications. The program supports the realization of projects by artists\, o
 rganizations\, and institutions with a meaningful connection to Latin Amer
 ica. This is the 4th edition of the grants\; the Foundation receives appli
 cations via its online platform from 7 July to 9 September 2026. ELIGIBILI
 TY: artists\, collectives\, art professionals\, non-profit organizations\,
  institutions\, and foundations with a significant connection to Latin Ame
 rica\, whether through nationality\, cultural heritage\, and/or the locati
 on where the project will take place. Refer to the Terms and Conditions do
 cument on the website for full details. Inquiries: info@fundacionamaamoedo
 .org. Application deadline: Wednesday 9 September 2026\, 11:59 pm.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Fundacion Ama Amoedo\nLocation: Open to applicants with a signif
 icant connection to Latin America\, through nationality\, cultural heritag
 e\, and/or the location where the project takes place.\nAward: Ten grants 
 of USD 10\,000 each\, awarded annually across four categories: Artists\, A
 rt and Social Engagement\, Organizations\, and Publications. No applicatio
 n fee mentioned.\nDuration: Applications accepted via the online platform 
 from 7 July to 9 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://www.fundacionamaamoedo.o
 rg/programas/becas?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://www.fundacionamaamoedo.org/programas/becas?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open to applicants with a significant connection to Latin America\
 , through nationality\, cultural heritage\, and/or the location where the 
 project takes place.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arts-council-ireland-visual-arts-project-award-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260723
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260724
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council of Ireland: Visual Arts Project Award 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Arts Council of Ireland's Visual Arts Project Award funds p
 rofessional visual artists\, curators\, and producers to develop and deliv
 er visual arts projects\, in three strands: planning and pre-production (u
 p to EUR 12\,000)\, production and engagement (up to EUR 60\,000)\, and pa
 rtnership production (up to EUR 150\,000). Primarily aimed at applicants b
 ased in the Republic of Ireland\, but the Arts Council's standard eligibil
 ity clause allows applicants based elsewhere where the application explici
 tly demonstrates how the outcomes will benefit the arts in Ireland. The wi
 der Project Award 2027 covers nine disciplines including film and music on
  a similar timeline. Deadline 23 July 2026\, 17:30 Irish time.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Arts Council of Ireland / An Chomhairle Ealaion\nLocation: Republic 
 of Ireland. Applicants based outside Ireland may apply if the application 
 clearly shows how outcomes benefit the arts in the Republic of Ireland.\nA
 ward: Three strands: up to EUR 12\,000 (planning and pre-production)\, up 
 to EUR 60\,000 (production and engagement)\, up to EUR 150\,000 (partnersh
 ip production). No application fee.\nDuration: Projects delivered in 2027.
 \n\nMore: https://artscouncil.ie/funding-opportunities/project-award/visua
 l-arts-project-award/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://artscouncil.ie/funding-opportunities/project-award/visual-arts-
 project-award/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Republic of Ireland. Applicants based outside Ireland may apply if
  the application clearly shows how outcomes benefit the arts in the Republ
 ic of Ireland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ctm-2027-radio-lab-in-listening@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: In Listening 2027: Call for Hybrid Radio/Live Works (CTM 
 Festival\, Berlin)
DESCRIPTION:In Listening is the renamed successor to the CTM Radio Lab\, af
 ter more than a decade of collaboration between CTM Festival and Germany's
  public radio Deutschlandfunk Kultur\, with support from Austria's ORF\, z
 eroing in on sound-focused experiences. This open call is for works strong
 ly grounded in experimental sound practices and audio art and driven by co
 nceptual approaches or sonic narratives\, exploring the blurred edges betw
 een sound\, noise\, music\, storytelling\, poetry\, and documenting\, wher
 e sound is the main medium. Works should respond to the CTM 2027 theme 'Pr
 ocess...ing'\, with active listening informing the proposals. Applications
  should describe how the work could be developed for two complementary out
 puts: a LIVE EVENT at CTM 2027 and a RADIO BROADCAST on Deutschlandfunk Ku
 ltur and Oe1/ORF. At CTM\, works are presented in the silent green Kuppelh
 alle with an intimate setup\, the audience seated around the performer(s) 
 and surrounded by a 6.1-channel PA (creative use of fewer channels\, stere
 o\, or mono is welcome\; minimal lighting and scenography or performances 
 in the dark are suitable\, but video and complex scenography are out of sc
 ope). For radio/podcast\, proposals should consider the individual listeni
 ng experience (a recording of the performance is not sufficient)\; the bro
 adcast is a 40-55 minute piece aired in a late-night slot to a largely Ger
 man-speaking\, non-specialist audience. Works premiere at CTM 2027 (22-31 
 January 2027\, Berlin)\, are broadcast in Deutschlandfunk Kultur's Klangku
 nst programme in Spring 2027\, and presented via ORF (Oe1 Zeit-Ton or Blau
 e Stunde / Kunstradio) and/or ORF musikprotokoll im steirischen herbst in 
 Graz (Autumn 2027)\, then available for streaming for at least one year. B
 UDGET: two selected works each receive EUR 6\,000\; winners give up to two
  performances at CTM. Group proposals are possible but should keep a modes
 t travel budget. JURY: Jan Rohlf (CTM)\, Marcus Gammel (Deutschlandfunk Ku
 ltur)\, Anna Soucek (ORF Oe1)\, and one independent artist. TIMELINE: dead
 line 6 September 2026 at 23:59 Berlin time\; winners announced mid-October
  2026\; remote production late October 2026 to January 2027. APPLY (in Eng
 lish\, PDF\, max 20MB) with a project description including rough budget (
 max 4 pages)\, technical requirements\, and CV\; questions to in_listening
 @ctm-festival.de. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: CTM Festival with D
 eutschlandfunk Kultur and ORF\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany. Premiered at CT
 M 2027 and broadcast on Deutschlandfunk Kultur\, with onward presentation 
 via ORF Oe1 (Zeit-Ton or Blaue Stunde / Kunstradio) and/or ORF musikprotok
 oll im steirischen herbst in Graz. Applications accepted internationally\,
  submitted in English.\nAward: Two selected works are each supported by a 
 fee of EUR 6\,000. CTM covers travel to Berlin and lodging during the prod
 uction and festival periods\; technical and staging costs for the CTM pres
 entation (and possible ORF musikprotokoll presentation) are covered separa
 tely by arrangement. Research\, creation and collaborator costs are the ar
 tist's own. Radio-production support (translations\, voiceovers\, studio t
 ime) can be provided by Deutschlandfunk Kultur upon discussion. No applica
 tion fee.\nDuration: Work premiered at CTM Festival 22-31 January 2027\; r
 adio broadcast Spring 2027\; ORF/musikprotokoll presentation Autumn 2027. 
 Remote production phase late October 2026 to January 2027.\n\nMore: https:
 //www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/in-listening-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/in-listening-2027?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. Premiered at CTM 2027 and broadcast on Deutschla
 ndfunk Kultur\, with onward presentation via ORF Oe1 (Zeit-Ton or Blaue St
 unde / Kunstradio) and/or ORF musikprotokoll im steirischen herbst in Graz
 . Applications accepted internationally\, submitted in English.
END:VEVENT
