UID:south-arts-emerging-traditional-artists-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Emerging Traditional Artists Program 2026
DESCRIPTION:South Arts' Emerging Traditional Artists Program supports folk 
 and traditional artists in the early stages of their careers with USD 5\,0
 00 each\, plus professional development workshops and peer mentorship at n
 o cost. The money is for learning: training\, networking and promotion. Re
 cipients also record an interview about their art practice. ELIGIBILITY: i
 ndividual practitioners early in their careers\, at least 18 by the deadli
 ne\, US citizens or lawfully authorised residents\, who have lived for at 
 least two years in designated Appalachian Regional Commission or Delta Reg
 ional Authority counties within Alabama\, Georgia\, Kentucky\, Louisiana\,
  Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina or Tennessee\, or who are m
 embers of state or federally recognised Native American tribes. Applicants
  must demonstrate a high level of skill in\, commitment to\, and leadershi
 p in their traditional art form. Deadline 30 September 2026 at 5:00pm ET.\
 n\nOrganisation: South Arts\nLocation: Designated Appalachian Regional Com
 mission and Delta Regional Authority counties in Alabama\, Georgia\, Kentu
 cky\, Louisiana\, Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina and Tennes
 see\, USA.\nAward: USD 5\,000 per awardee\, paid as a single lump sum at t
 he start of the award period\, to fund learning opportunities including tr
 aining\, networking and promotion. Recipients also take part in virtual wo
 rkshops and peer mentorship at no cost\, and record an interview about the
 ir practice. No application fee.\nDuration: Award period with accompanying
  workshops and peer mentorship\n\nMore: https://www.southarts.org/grants-o
 pportunities/emerging-traditional-artists-program?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.southarts.org/grants-opportunities/emerging-traditional-art
 ists-program?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Designated Appalachian Regional Commission and Delta Regional Auth
 ority counties in Alabama\, Georgia\, Kentucky\, Louisiana\, Mississippi\,
  North Carolina\, South Carolina and Tennessee\, USA.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:south-arts-arts-in-community-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts in Community Grants 2027
DESCRIPTION:South Arts' Arts in Community Grants fund artist fees for commu
 nity engagement projects featuring visiting Southern artists. Each funded 
 project must include both a public presentation and an educational or comm
 unity engagement component\, so this is not a straight presenting grant. U
 p to USD 10\,000 is available per project against a dollar-for-dollar cash
  match\, with a minimum artist fee of USD 4\,000 and a minimum request of 
 USD 2\,000. ELIGIBILITY: tax-exempt 501(c)(3) nonprofit arts organizations
 \, official units of local\, county or state government\, and federally re
 cognised tribal communities with nonprofit status\, located in the nine-st
 ate South Arts region (Alabama\, Florida\, Georgia\, Kentucky\, Louisiana\
 , Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina and Tennessee). Applicants
  must have a Unique Entity Identifier (UEI). Applications opened 15 July 2
 026\; applicants are notified by email by 24 November 2026\, and grants ar
 e subject to funding availability. Projects must take place between 1 Janu
 ary 2027 and 31 December 2027. Deadline Tuesday 1 September 2026 at 11:59p
 m ET.\n\nOrganisation: South Arts\nLocation: USA\, nine-state South Arts r
 egion: Alabama\, Florida\, Georgia\, Kentucky\, Louisiana\, Mississippi\, 
 North Carolina\, South Carolina and Tennessee.\nAward: Up to USD 10\,000 p
 er project\, covering artist fees. A dollar-for-dollar cash match is requi
 red\, so a USD 10\,000 request needs USD 10\,000 in matching funds. Minimu
 m artist fee is USD 4\,000 and the minimum grant request is USD 2\,000. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Projects must take place between 1 January 20
 27 and 31 December 2027\n\nMore: https://www.southarts.org/grants-opportun
 ities/arts-community-grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://www.southarts.org/grants-opportunities/arts-community-grants?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA\, nine-state South Arts region: Alabama\, Florida\, Georgia\, 
 Kentucky\, Louisiana\, Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina and T
 ennessee.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:south-arts-literary-arts-project-grants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261007
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261008
SUMMARY:Deadline: Literary Arts Project Grants 2027
DESCRIPTION:South Arts' Literary Arts Project Grants fund up to USD 5\,000 
 for the creation and publishing of creative literary work (journals\, book
 s\, anthologies) and for community engagement projects such as reading ser
 ies\, festivals and podcasts. Eligible expenses include personnel\, artist
  fees\, editorial services\, travel\, marketing\, facility rental and insu
 rance. ELIGIBILITY: independent nonprofit literary arts organizations\, in
 dependent publishers\, and small presses including literary journals\, hea
 dquartered in the nine-state South Arts region (Alabama\, Florida\, Georgi
 a\, Kentucky\, Louisiana\, Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina a
 nd Tennessee) with an established literary arts mission. This is an organi
 zational grant\, not an individual one\; individual writers should look at
  the Southern Prize for Literature instead. Applications opened 12 August 
 2026\; award notifications in November 2026\, with a final report due 30 J
 une 2027\, and all expenses must occur between 1 July 2026 and 30 June 202
 7. Deadline 7 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: South Arts\nLocation: USA\, n
 ine-state South Arts region: Alabama\, Florida\, Georgia\, Kentucky\, Loui
 siana\, Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina and Tennessee.\nAwar
 d: Up to USD 5\,000 per project. Eligible expenses include personnel\, art
 ist fees\, editorial services\, travel\, marketing\, facility rental and i
 nsurance. No application fee.\nDuration: All expenses must occur between 1
  July 2026 and 30 June 2027\n\nMore: https://www.southarts.org/grants-oppo
 rtunities/literary-arts-project-grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.southarts.org/grants-opportunities/literary-arts-project-gr
 ants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:USA\, nine-state South Arts region: Alabama\, Florida\, Georgia\, 
 Kentucky\, Louisiana\, Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina and T
 ennessee.
