BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:community-engagement-artists-creatives-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Artists and Creatives Grant\, Fall 2026
DESCRIPTION:Community Engagement\, a 501(c)(3) nonprofit based in Orange Co
 unty\, California\, funds independent creatives making or presenting work 
 that relates to or encourages community engagement. Its framing is collabo
 rative placemaking\, projects from communal gardens to public mosaics to i
 ntergenerational art activities that reimagine shared spaces and stimulate
  social engagement\, creative expression and collective empowerment\, with
  a focus on diverse and underserved neighbourhoods. GEOGRAPHY DEPENDS ON T
 HE ROUND: the fall round\, deadline 15 September\, is open only to artists
  living or working in California. The spring round\, deadline 15 March\, i
 s open to artists living or working anywhere in the US. WHAT IT FUNDS: the
  execution of community-engaged projects\, prioritising the creation of ne
 w artworks that present new and imaginative possibilities. The funder says
  it is not likely to fund art classes\, take-home art kits\, or exhibition
 s of studio artwork in preexisting galleries unless the proposal centres a
  clear and purposeful collaboration with a community. WHO CAN APPLY: indiv
 idual artists and artist collectives\, including collaborators. NOT SUPPOR
 TED: arts festivals\, nonprofit and for-profit organizations\, student pro
 jects (undergraduate or graduate)\, residencies\, research symposia\, stud
 io rent\, conferences\, theaters\, and any activity affiliated with religi
 ous organizations. Successful grantees must wait at least two years before
  reapplying. The grant explicitly encourages applications from artists his
 torically underrepresented in the arts\, including Black\, Indigenous\, Pe
 ople of Color\, Queer\, Trans\, Deaf\, Disabled\, Immigrant\, Refugee and 
 Self-Taught artists. HOW TO APPLY: upload four PDFs to a single publicly a
 ccessible online folder (Google Drive\, Dropbox or similar) and submit the
  link via the form\; documents not in PDF format will not be considered. A
 pplications that do not follow the guidelines are not reviewed\, and if yo
 u have not heard back six weeks after the deadline the application was uns
 uccessful. Deadline 15 September 2026 at 11:59pm PST\, with decisions 15 O
 ctober.\n\nOrganisation: Community Engagement\nLocation: California\, USA 
 for the fall round. The spring round (March deadline) is open to artists l
 iving or working anywhere in the US.\nAward: Usually USD 500 to USD 2\,500
 \, and in rare circumstances up to USD 5\,000. The funder suggests most ar
 tists apply for under USD 2\,500 unless advised otherwise. No application 
 fee.\nDuration: Project-based grant\n\nMore: https://www.communityengageme
 nt.org/how-to-apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.communityengagement.org/how-to-apply?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:California\, USA for the fall round. The spring round (March deadl
 ine) is open to artists living or working anywhere in the US.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:adagp-sgdl-arcane-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arcane Grant 2026 for Artist Books
DESCRIPTION:Artists' books get little support\, financially or in distribut
 ion\, despite their place in art history and in the careers of the people 
 who make them. ADAGP\, the French collecting society for copyright in the 
 visual arts\, and SGDL\, the French society of authors\, created the Arcan
 e grant in response: EUR 9\,000 to one winning project for the conception 
 and production of an artist's book made collaboratively by a visual artist
  and a writer. WHO CAN APPLY: a pair consisting of a professional visual a
 rtist from the French scene (working or residing in France for at least fi
 ve years\, or a French national living abroad) and a French-language autho
 r working in fiction\, non-fiction\, poetry\, children's literature or the
 atre who has already been published by a publisher. A trio is also possibl
 e where a publishing structure joins the project. WHAT COUNTS AS AN ARTIST
 'S BOOK: a creation\, a work of art in book form\, in a limited print run 
 of between 1 and 500 copies\, which may be signed or numbered. Explicitly 
 not eligible: magazines\, fanzines\, limited editions of an ordinary book\
 , and any publication that simply presents an artist's work\, such as mono
 graphs or illustrated books. APPLICATION: the file must be in French and i
 ncludes a jointly written project presentation of up to three pages coveri
 ng the artistic and editorial vision\, constituent elements\, methods of r
 ealisation and desired final form\; a one-page technical sheet giving titl
 e\, print run\, format\, page count\, paper quality\, printing techniques 
 and materials\; a provisional timetable\; and a detailed balanced provisio
 nal budget of expenses and financing. Artistic elements are a CV of exhibi
 tions and publications (2 pages) and a portfolio with website link (10 pag
 es) for the artist\, a CV and website link for the author (2 pages)\, and 
 a one-page editorial line for the publishing structure if there is one\; c
 ontact details must be omitted from these. Administrative elements are swo
 rn declarations that the project is a new creation with copyright held sol
 ely by the pair\, that the artist is from the French scene\, and\, if appl
 icable\, that the publishing structure undertakes to publish the work. Tem
 plates are downloadable from the Required Documents page. TIMELINE: call l
 aunched 7 July 2026\, applications close 7 September 2026 at 2pm\, jury me
 ets November 2026\, winner announced end of November 2026\, and the work m
 ust be published within two years of that announcement. The regulations mu
 st be read before applying\, and submitting an application constitutes acc
 eptance of them. Contact: arcane@adagp.fr.\n\nOrganisation: ADAGP and SGDL
  (Societe des Gens de Lettres)\nLocation: France. Open to a professional v
 isual artist from the French scene (working or residing in France for at l
 east five years\, or of French nationality living abroad) paired with a Fr
 ench-language author.\nAward: EUR 9\,000 to the single winning project\, s
 upporting the conception and production of an artist's book. NOTE ON TAX: 
 ADAGP grants count as primary artistic income under the French Intellectua
 l Property Code (art. L112-2)\, so the sum falls under the artist-author s
 ocial security and tax regime\, subject to URSSAF contributions and income
  tax declared as non-commercial profits (micro-BNC or controlled declarati
 on). VAT is not due. No application fee.\nDuration: The winning duo or tri
 o commits to publishing the artist's book within two years of the announce
 ment\n\nMore: https://candidatures.adagp.fr/en/?option=com_emundus&view=pr
 ogramme&cid=187&Itemid=1531&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://candidatures.adagp.fr/en/?option=com_emundus&view=programme&cid
 =187&Itemid=1531&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:France. Open to a professional visual artist from the French scene
  (working or residing in France for at least five years\, or of French nat
 ionality living abroad) paired with a French-language author.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:linz-kultur-arbeitsstipendien-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Linz Kultur Working Grants 2026 (Arbeitsstipendien)
DESCRIPTION:The city of Linz awards project-related working grants to susta
 in and develop its art scene\, in line with the Linz cultural development 
 plan and the city's status as a UNESCO City of Media Arts. The stated aims
  are enabling the further development of artistic practice\, supporting ar
 tistic careers\, and securing a professional artistic existence and innova
 tive production in Linz. Each scholarship is worth EUR 5\,000 over five mo
 nths\, with EUR 30\,000 available in total this year. DISCIPLINES: fine ar
 ts and photography\, literature\, music\, performing arts\, interdisciplin
 ary art forms\, media art and film. WHAT TO SUBMIT: a concrete artistic pr
 oject\, which may be an independent work\, a series of works\, or the cont
 inuation of an earlier series or project. Preparatory work and concept pha
 ses are also eligible. Projects already funded by the City of Linz cannot 
 be submitted\, and only one submission per person per year is permitted. E
 LIGIBILITY: artists of any citizenship who can demonstrate that their cent
 re of work is in Linz\, in the form of a permanent site for their artistic
  work\, and who have a sufficient connection to the city. SELECTION CRITER
 IA: the expert jury assesses sufficient Linz connection\, innovative artis
 tic potential\, independent artistic expression\, a clearly recognisable c
 onception of the artistic intention in the proposal\, and the quality and 
 continuity of the artistic work. REPORTING OBLIGATION: within three months
  of the scholarship ending\, a written progress report of 1\,800 to 5\,400
  characters including spaces must be submitted with supporting documentati
 on\, and after review it is published on the City of Linz website. The pro
 ject need not be finished\, but significant progress must be evident. If n
 o report is submitted\, or the report shows insufficient progress\, the sc
 holarship must be repaid under the City of Linz General Funding Guidelines
 . REQUIRED DOCUMENTS: the completed online application form\, a project de
 scription of up to 10 pages including the innovative approach and planned 
 schedule\, a biography with catalogue of works and any exhibition or prese
 ntation list\, an artistic portfolio\, and references and press reviews. N
 OTE: the online form and the call documents are in German. Contact: lkf.kb
 @mag.linz.at. Deadline 7 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: City of Linz (Li
 nz Kultur\, Arts and Cultural Funding Department)\nLocation: Linz\, Austri
 a. Open to artists of any citizenship whose centre of work is in Linz.\nAw
 ard: EUR 5\,000 per scholarship over a five-month period\, from a total po
 t of EUR 30\,000 this year\, so approximately six grants. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: Five months\n\nMore: https://www.linz.at/serviceguide/viewc
 hapter.php?chapter_id=123406&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://www.linz.at/serviceguide/viewchapter.php?chapter_id=123406&utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Linz\, Austria. Open to artists of any citizenship whose centre of
  work is in Linz.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:epic-megagrants-cycle-2-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Deadline: Epic MegaGrants 2026 (Cycle 2)
DESCRIPTION:Epic MegaGrants are financial grants from Epic Games for creati
 ve\, noteworthy and innovative projects built in and around Unreal Engine\
 , or projects that enhance the open source 3D graphics ecosystem. Over 2\,
 000 grants have been awarded to date. The programme is explicitly aimed at
  smaller teams\, solo developers and individuals as well as studios: Epic 
 states that individuals and small teams are eligible and encouraged\, and 
 that it treats every project equally regardless of who you are. WHAT IS FU
 NDED: (1) INDIE GAMES\, small or solo teams working in Unreal Engine\, sub
 mitted past the idea and design phase with at least some working prototype
 \, ideally with a video link\; (2) UEFN EXPERIENCES\, Fortnite Creative is
 lands and interactive experiences built in Unreal Editor for Fortnite\; (3
 ) ENGINE MIGRATION\, a proportion of MegaGrants is reserved for teams movi
 ng a partially developed project from another engine to Unreal\; (4) FILM\
 , TV AND LIVE EVENTS\, including live-action and animated films and shows\
 , broadcast\, live and location-based events\; (5) OTHER NON-GAMES VERTICA
 LS such as architecture\, automotive\, manufacturing\, simulation\, produc
 t design\, advertising and VR/AR\, where more detailed project plans and p
 rototypes are expected\; (6) EDUCATION\, including research\, curricula an
 d course development and university programmes\, though for institutions E
 pic accepts submissions only from degree-granting schools and educators at
  such schools\; (7) TOOLS AND OPEN SOURCE\, creating open source tools or 
 enhancing open source software using Unreal Engine. NON-UNREAL PROJECTS AR
 E ELIGIBLE if you want to move them to Unreal Engine\, or if the project e
 nhances open source 3D content creation whether or not it relates to Unrea
 l Engine. EVALUATION rests on three things: quality and unique appeal (hig
 h-quality demos or builds\, well-documented descriptions\, technical ambit
 ion)\; community benefit (how you will give back\, for example open-sourci
 ng the project\, releasing assets through a marketplace\, sharing learning
 s\, or shipping an SDK\, tool or plug-in)\; and viability (a clear budget 
 with major spend areas and a project plan with milestones\, deliverables a
 nd timeline). NOTE ON DEADLINES: the FAQ still describes MegaGrants as an 
 ongoing programme with no specific deadline\, but the timeline published o
 n the same page now runs in fixed cycles\, and the Cycle 2 submission wind
 ow closes 4 September 2026 at 23:59 ET. Treat the cycle date as the operat
 ive deadline. You may apply for more than one project\, and may reapply fo
 r the same project after a decision if you have made updates. Epic is not 
 offering sponsorships and cannot give feedback on applications. Apply at m
 egagrants.unrealengine.com.\n\nOrganisation: Epic Games\nLocation: Open wo
 rldwide. Epic states that if it can legally make payment to you\, you are 
 eligible.\nAward: Typical grants range from USD 5\,000 to USD 75\,000\, wi
 th some exceptional projects receiving up to USD 150\,000. Epic states tha
 t recipients continue to own their IP and may publish it however they wish
 \, so this is a grant rather than an investment or equity deal. Grants up 
 to and including USD 25\,000 may be paid in a single instalment\; larger g
 rants are paid across several instalments tied to continued progress. Fund
 s are for project and team expenses such as development and hiring\; hardw
 are purchases or rentals are approved only occasionally\, case by case. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Cycle 2 of 2026 runs 29 June to 11 December 2
 026. Submission window 29 June to 4 September 2026 (closes 23:59 ET)\, rev
 iew 5 September to 4 December 2026\, notices 7 to 11 December 2026. Cycle 
 1 ran 12 January to 19 June 2026.\n\nMore: https://www.unrealengine.com/me
 gagrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.unrealengine.com/megagrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open worldwide. Epic states that if it can legally make payment to
  you\, you are eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:africa-no-filter-voices-for-climate-justice-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: Africa No Filter: Voices for Climate Justice 2026
DESCRIPTION:Voices for Climate Justice supports African storytellers making
  work about how climate finance reaches the continent as debt rather than 
 as grants. The framing of the call: African nations are being pushed furth
 er into debt through loans despite the continent's minimal contribution to
  the crisis\, with many governments spending more on debt repayment than o
 n health and climate adaptation combined. WHO IT IS FOR: journalists\, con
 tent creators\, podcasters\, vloggers\, muralists and data visualizers. WH
 AT YOU GET: a 12-month programme delivered with Comic Relief giving 15 to 
 20 storytellers training in climate justice\, data storytelling and narrat
 ive framing\, then mentorship and work with researchers and partners to de
 velop accurate\, research-based stories\, plus content amplification and g
 rants of up to USD 4\,000. ELIGIBILITY: aged 18 or over\; based in one of 
 the ten listed countries\; an active and highly engaged platform (podcast\
 , YouTube channel\, TikTok\, Facebook\, Instagram\, publication or data vi
 sualization portfolio) running for more than a year\; a combined audience 
 of 5\,000 or more followers across Instagram\, TikTok\, Facebook\, Twitter
 /X and Snapchat for content creators and data visualizers\, while journali
 sts may instead demonstrate reach through publication circulation\; conten
 t creators must be unsigned and not represented by an agent\, though journ
 alists may be affiliated with a publication provided the submitted work an
 d content rights remain their own\; a commitment to publishing at least fo
 ur pieces on gender\, debt and fossil fuels over at least six months\; and
  individual applicants only\, no organisations or agencies. Proposals must
  focus on the campaign's core themes of climate justice\, gender\, debt an
 d fossil fuels in Africa. NOT CONSIDERED: incomplete applications\, postal
  or email submissions\, hacked material\, vulgar\, racist\, sexist or homo
 phobic material\, work reinforcing stereotypes of Africa as poor\, corrupt
 \, diseased\, conflict-ridden or lacking agency\, and accounts or posts bo
 osted by paid engagement. HOW TO APPLY: prepare a pitch deck of no more th
 an 5 slides or a video of no more than 60 seconds connecting gender\, debt
  and fossil fuels in Africa\, then submit through the ANF application port
 al with links to your platforms and a short description of the audience yo
 u plan to reach. Content may be delivered in English or French. Selection 
 weighs originality of the idea\, relevance to ANF's mission of storytellin
 g beyond stereotypes\, relevance to the gender-debt-fossil fuel focus\, an
 d reach or standing on your platform or in your community. Only shortliste
 d candidates are notified.\n\nOrganisation: Africa No Filter\, in partners
 hip with Comic Relief\nLocation: Applicants must be based in Mozambique\, 
 Uganda\, Nigeria\, Angola\, Chad\, the Republic of Congo\, Tanzania\, Sout
 h Sudan\, Malawi or Zambia.\nAward: Grants of up to USD 4\,000 (the call s
 tates a range of USD 0 to 4\,000)\, alongside training\, mentorship and co
 ntent amplification. Between 15 and 20 storytellers will be supported. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: 12-month programme. Applications opened 11 Aug
 ust 2026 and are reviewed on a rolling basis\; deadline 25 September 2026 
 at 18:00 GMT. Screening 5 October\, interviews 9 October\, outcomes commun
 icated in the first week of October and grantees announced 15 October 2026
 .\n\nMore: https://africanofilter.org/what-we-do/community/voices-for-clim
 ate-justice/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://africanofilter.org/what-we-do/community/voices-for-climate-just
 ice/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must be based in Mozambique\, Uganda\, Nigeria\, Angola
 \, Chad\, the Republic of Congo\, Tanzania\, South Sudan\, Malawi or Zambi
 a.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:africa-no-filter-kekere-storytellers-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260828T132446Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Africa No Filter: Kekere Storytellers Fund 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Kekere Storytellers Fund pays micro-grants to emerging Afri
 can storytellers who are already creating and publishing work that offers 
 fresh and alternative perspectives on the continent\, showing an Africa th
 at is innovative\, evolving and creative rather than defined by poverty\, 
 conflict\, disease\, poor leadership and corruption. Africa No Filter desc
 ribes the fund as its way of getting funding\, which is limited and rarely
  accessed by up-and-coming storytellers\, to artists\, journalists and con
 tent creators. PREREQUISITE: applicants must first be members of Africa No
  Filter's African Narrative Collective\, so join that before applying. ELI
 GIBILITY: African\, based anywhere in Africa or the diaspora\; under 35\; 
 able to work in English or French\; a track record of ground-breaking work
  that challenges stereotypical narratives about your community\, country o
 r the continent\; at least two years of related work experience\; a minimu
 m of 5\,000 followers across Twitter\, Facebook\, TikTok\, Instagram and Y
 ouTube\; and falling into at least one of two categories\, MEDIA AND CONTE
 NT CREATORS (journalist\, blogger\, vlogger\, podcaster\, fiction and non-
 fiction writer\, photographer) or ARTISTS (poet\, musician\, spoken word p
 oet\, dancer\, painter\, sculptor\, illustrator\, animator). NOT ELIGIBLE:
  filmmakers\, who are directed to ANF's Last Mile Film Fund instead\; stor
 ytellers without evidence of narrative-shifting work\; requests to buy equ
 ipment such as cameras or laptops\; and requests to host or attend events 
 such as workshops\, festivals or conferences. WHAT ANF IS LOOKING FOR: an 
 interesting\, unique story about Africa that amplifies unheard voices\, ch
 allenges global perspectives and introduces contemporary narratives\, with
  a clear sense of what you want the reader or viewer to take away and the 
 impact you want to create locally and globally.\n\nOrganisation: Africa No
  Filter\nLocation: Africans based anywhere in Africa or the diaspora.\nAwa
 rd: Micro-grants of USD 500 to USD 3\,000. Between 12 and 14 storytellers 
 will be selected. No application fee.\nDuration: Rolling. Applications sta
 y open until the end of the year or until 12 to 14 storytellers have been 
 selected\, whichever comes first\, so apply early rather than close to the
  nominal end date.\n\nMore: https://africanofilter.org/what-we-do/communit
 y/kekere-storytellers-fund/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://africanofilter.org/what-we-do/community/kekere-storytellers-fun
 d/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Africans based anywhere in Africa or the diaspora.
END:VEVENT
